DATASET : https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/paramaggarwal/fashion-product-images-dataset

I used a combination of two file types: PNG images for the visual data and a styles.csv file for the associated metadata. Each row in the CSV is
  linked to an image through a unique ID that matches the image filename, which makes it easy to map features to the corresponding pictures.
  I chose this approach because the dataset also provides JSON files, but they are large in number and size, with one JSON file per image.
  These files contain not only information specific to each picture but also additional metadata that is not necessary for this project.
  Although this extra information could be useful for other applications or more advanced feature extraction tasks, working with JSON would require processing each file
  individually, which is less efficient. In contrast, the CSV file consolidates all image metadata into a single structured file, making it much easier and faster to access and process.
